  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760309,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1988 B.C. - Commodore 64\n\nJourney back to the dawn of civilization in *1988 B.C.*, a captivating strategy and simulation game for the Commodore 64!  Taking on the role of a tribal leader, you must guide your people from a small settlement to a thriving empire across a dynamic, procedurally generated landscape.  \n\nThe game blends resource management with strategic decision-making.  Gather food, mine stone, and craft tools to expand your village, research new technologies, and build a powerful army.  Face challenges like harsh weather, dwindling resources, and the threat of rival tribes, all while striving to improve the happiness and prosperity of your population. \n\n*1988 B.C.* features a unique \"time-pressure\" mechanic – seasons change, and you must adapt to survive.  Diplomacy, trade, and warfare are all viable paths to dominance.  Will you forge alliances, conquer your enemies, or focus on peaceful development?  The fate of your tribe rests in your hands! Experience the thrill of building a civilization from the ground up in this engaging and historically-inspired adventure."
    },
